# WAAMTO Enterprise Performance & Token Rules v3.0

> Mandatory performance and token optimization rules for all WAAMTO ecosystem projects.

---

# Purpose

Optimize AI efficiency without reducing development quality, correctness, testing or security.

Performance optimization must never create incomplete implementations.

---

# Core Principle

Read everything reasonably required.

Never read unrelated code.

Optimize for intelligent analysis, not minimal analysis.

---

# Token Strategy

Always:

- Understand the task first.
- Identify affected modules.
- Read required dependencies.
- Ignore unrelated areas.
- Reuse previous context whenever possible.

---

# Repository Navigation

Prefer targeted navigation.

Avoid repository-wide exploration unless explicitly requested.

If multiple implementations exist, inspect only the most relevant ones.

---

# File Reading

Read:

- affected files
- direct dependencies
- shared utilities when required
- middleware when required
- services when required
- database layer when required
- API contracts when required

Avoid unrelated folders.

---

# Context Reuse

Never repeat analysis already completed during the same task.

Reuse previous understanding whenever safe.

---

# Search Strategy

Prefer:

- exact filename
- exact component
- exact function
- exact API
- exact class

Avoid broad keyword searches unless necessary.

---

# Code Generation

Generate only code required for the requested task.

Avoid unnecessary boilerplate.

Reuse existing patterns.

---

# Performance

Prefer:

- existing components
- shared libraries
- existing utilities

Avoid duplicate implementations.

---

# Testing

Run only validation reasonably required by the current task.

Do not skip dependency validation.

Do not run unrelated system-wide testing.

---

# Browser Usage

Use browser only for:

- UI validation
- production verification
- external integrations
- user-requested checks

---

# Terminal Usage

Run only commands that provide value for the requested task.

Avoid unnecessary installs, builds and long-running processes.

---

# Communication

Keep reports concise.

Focus on:

- work completed
- files changed
- validation
- remaining issues

Avoid repeating analysis.

---

